char/krzysztof_intro	Right. New day. Same bench. Let's not make it worse than it has to be.
char/krzysztof_mutter1	I don't even like drinking, you know. ...Go on then. One.
char/krzysztof_mutter2	Be nice to people. Most of them are bastards, but you never know which ones.
char/krzysztof_name	Krzysztof
char/krzysztof_quirk	Calm, decent, helpful to a fault. Swears blind he doesn't drink, then drinks. Everyone likes him, which on this street is deeply suspicious.
char/krzysztof_story1	Krzysztof had a flat, a job, and a woman he'd have walked into traffic for.
char/krzysztof_story2	So when she needed money, he gave her all of it. Then a bit more. Then the rent.
char/krzysztof_story3	She left anyway, with a bloke who owned two cars. The bank took the flat.
char/krzysztof_story4	Now he's the calmest man on the street. He's already lost the one thing he cared about, and everything since is just weather. Press Enter to become him.
char/marcin_intro	Head like a bin lorry reversing. Where's the nearest bottle, and who do I have to fight for it.
char/marcin_mutter1	Who needs her. The bench never left me for a prick called Darek.
char/marcin_mutter2	I'm not drunk. I'm emotionally efficient. There's a difference.
char/marcin_name	Marcin
char/marcin_quirk	Just got dumped and he's taking it like a champion, meaning terribly. Drinks with anyone, and if you say no he takes it personal. Sees a copper, loses his mind.
char/marcin_story1	Marcin was doing fine, right up until she said the words 'we need to talk.'
char/marcin_story2	That was three weeks and two hundred bottles ago. He is not bitter. He'll tell you he's not bitter, loudly, to strangers, at eleven in the morning.
char/marcin_story3	He hates the police because a copper once told him to move along on the worst night of his life.
char/marcin_story4	He's decided to take that personally until the day he dies. Press Enter to become him.
char/sebastian_intro	Today I sort my life out. Today. Definitely. Right after this one last thing.
char/sebastian_mutter1	One more sale and I go straight. Said that Tuesday. And the Tuesday before that.
char/sebastian_mutter2	I could get a proper job. I'd be brilliant at it. Probably. Shut up.
char/sebastian_name	Sebastian
char/sebastian_quirk	Wants a normal life, genuinely tries for one, then funds it by dealing, which torpedoes the normal life. Round and round the plughole he goes.
char/sebastian_story1	Sebastian's family gave him every chance, and a fair bit of grief to go with it.
char/sebastian_story2	One day the grief won and he packed a bag. He's clever, charming, and violently allergic to a normal life.
char/sebastian_story3	He deals a bit to get by, and swears every single week that it's the last time.
char/sebastian_story4	He genuinely believes it. That belief is the most valuable thing he owns. Press Enter to become him.
char/tom_intro	Still here. Still no passport. A degree in English Literature and I'm negotiating with a pigeon. Marvellous.
char/tom_mutter1	I have a degree, I'll have you know. Worth exactly one bottle in this economy.
char/tom_mutter2	Came here for love. Left with a bench. Well. Didn't leave. That's rather the whole problem.
char/tom_name	Tom
char/tom_quirk	English teacher. Came over chasing love, got battered by football lads, lost his passport, lost the plot. Now he's stranded on a bench in a country he can't spell.
char/tom_story1	Tom taught English in a nice quiet town, until his mates convinced him the love of his life was waiting out east.
char/tom_story2	He flew over full of hope and cheap aftershave.
char/tom_story3	He got as far as a stadium on match day, in entirely the wrong colours. Some gentlemen relieved him of his wallet, his phone, his passport, and two teeth.
char/tom_story4	Now he's on a bench, rehearsing the speech he'll give at the embassy, if he ever finds the embassy. Press Enter to become him.
