howto/sec_sleep	Getting your head down
howto/sec_town	Getting about the town
howto/sleep_1	A day ends when you sleep, and sleeping is your choice: walk onto a place you can kip and press Enter, and you will be asked whether you mean it.
howto/sleep_2	Your own block on ulica Wesoła is the good option. A door that locks, and you wake with the night behind you.
howto/sleep_3	You can also sleep rough: the bench in the park, behind the carpet beater in the courtyard, the end of the platform at the station. It costs you. Less of yourself back, a knock to your health, and the street may go through your pockets or take your bottles while you are under.
howto/sleep_4	Sleeping hungry sits with you all night. Sleeping blind drunk is its own reward in the morning.
howto/sleep_5	Going down having run yourself into the ground means you get less back. There is no way round that but to pace yourself.
howto/title	How to play. Up and down to read each line, Escape to go back.
howto/town_1	The town hangs off one main street, ulica Wesoła. North of it the park, south the courtyard behind the blocks, east the market, west the crossroads. The station is past the crossroads and the police station is somewhere you would rather not need.
howto/town_2	Exits are whole stretches of edge, so you walk off in the right direction and you are through. It announces where you have arrived. If you keep bumping into nothing, that is the edge of the area, not a wall, and it sounds lighter than one.
howto/town_3	Lost, which you will be: press T, pick a place, and it beeps toward it as you walk, quieter and lower when it is behind you, with a sound when you land on it. W reads the direction in words, as left, right, up and down. Those are the arrow keys, not which way you happen to be facing. It is the closest thing this game has to a map.
howto/town_4	Every area has its own sounds, placed where they actually are. A telly in a window, cars at the lights, the racket of the bar. Walk towards a sound and you are walking towards the thing making it.
howto/town_5	Anything behind you sounds slightly lower than it does in front of you, and lifts back to normal once you have turned to face it. That goes for people as well as places. It is how you tell what is still ahead of you from what you have already walked past.
howto/town_6	The music changes with the hour, so the street at seven in the morning is not the street at midnight. If it sounds uneasy, it is late, and being out late has its own consequences.
inv/bottles	Bottles: %1 of %2 you can carry.
inv/fag_one	a cigarette
inv/fags	Cigarettes: %1 left
inv/lighter_full	Lighter: plenty of gas left
inv/lighter_low	Lighter: running low, careful
inv/lighter_none	Lighter: none, or dead as a doornail
inv/money	Money: %1 złoty.
inv/sip_hint	Enter takes a sip or a bite. Keep pressing quickly and you will end up knocking it back.
inv/title	Your stuff. Up and down to look through it. I or Escape to close.
inv/trolley	Your trolley: %1.
jail/bring_something	Give him something you are carrying
jail/brought_drink	You get %1 through the bars somehow. He hides it before the officer turns round.
jail/brought_food	You pass %1 through the bars. He does not thank you, he just eats, and that is the thanks.
jail/leave_him	Say nothing and go
jail/left_him	You stand there a moment, say nothing, and go. He watches you the whole way out.
jail/mick	You take the mick out of him through the bars. His face changes, and it does not change back. That was cheap and you both know it.
jail/mick_grass	You put him in here and now you are laughing at him through the bars. Even the officer at the end of the corridor looks over at that.
jail/nobody_in	Both cells are empty today. The bars are open and the corridor smells of disinfectant and nothing else.
jail/nothing_to_bring	You pat your pockets and come up with nothing at all. You stand there with empty hands, which is its own kind of visit.
jail/say_sorry	Say you are sorry
jail/sees_you	%1 comes to the bars, surprised, and then genuinely pleased. Nobody visits. Nobody ever visits.
jail/sees_you_grass	%1 comes to the bars, sees who it is, and stops. There is a long silence. He knows exactly why he is in here, and so do you.
jail/sorry_grass	You say it. He does not say it is alright, because it is not. But he listens to the end, and that is more than you had any right to.
jail/sorry_ok	You tell him you are sorry he is in here. He shrugs like it is nothing and you both know it is not nothing. It counts, though. It counts a lot.
jail/take_the_mick	Take the mick out of him
jail/taken_in	They pick %1 up that same evening. Word goes round the estate before the van has left the street.
jail/what_do_you_do	What do you do?
jail/who_do_you_visit	Who are you here to see?
line/are_you_sure	Are you doing this?
line/do_it	Do it anyway
line/done	You raise your hand to %1. That is all it takes. One second, and the man you were this morning is gone.
line/thought_better	You unclench your hands and walk. Whatever else is true about you, that is still true.
line/town_turns	The street stops. Somebody is shouting. Somebody else is already on the phone. Every face you know is turned towards you and not one of them is on your side.
line/walk_away	Walk away
line/warn_child	You square up to %1 and the whole world goes quiet. She is a child. Sixteen. Whatever has happened to you, this is not who you are.
line/warn_woman	You square up to %1 and something in you goes very still. This is a line. You have never crossed it, and everyone on this street knows that about you.
look/area	You're in %1. Nothing right here. Walk around and explore, head to the edge to find an exit, or press T then W to track a spot.
marked/chat_1	Word gets round fast, and it got round about you. They tell you where to go, and they are not joking.
marked/chat_2	They see you coming and turn their back before you get a word out.
marked/chat_3	Not a chance. Not after that. They walk off mid sentence, and it was your sentence.
marked/counter_1	He takes your money and puts your change on the counter rather than in your hand. He does not say a word and he does not look up.
marked/counter_2	Whatever you were going to say, he is not having it. He serves you because that is the job, and that is the whole of it.
marked/counter_3	There is a silence over the counter that you could lean on. He has heard. Everyone has heard.
menu/continue	Continue
menu/continue_none	There's no saved game. You have nothing. Fitting, really.
menu/farewell_1	Right. The bench will still be there tomorrow. It always is.
menu/farewell_2	Off you go then. Mind how you go, and mind who you owe.
menu/farewell_3	That is you done. The bottles will keep.
menu/farewell_4	Go on then. Somebody has to be sober tonight and it may as well be you.
menu/farewell_5	Out you go. Try not to think about the trolley.
menu/farewell_6	See you tomorrow. The street is not going anywhere.
menu/farewell_7	Done for today. Wesoła will manage without you. Just about.
menu/farewell_8	Away you go. And if anybody asks, you were never here.
