shop/ask	What are you after?
shop/back	Back
shop/bought_beer_1	A cold beer. Civilised. Almost respectable.
shop/bought_beer_2	First beer of the day. Or the fifth. Who's counting.
shop/bought_beer_3	Beer. Crack, hiss, glug. The little things in life.
shop/bought_cheapwine_1	The cheap stuff in the plastic bottle. Regret and blackcurrant.
shop/bought_cheapwine_2	Fortified wine, barely. Tastes the way a park bench smells.
shop/bought_cheapwine_3	Cheap wine. Your teeth go purple and you stop caring.
shop/bought_coffee_1	You wrap both hands round the cup. It is too hot to drink and you drink it anyway.
shop/bought_coffee_2	Kiosk coffee: bitter, scalding, and exactly what you needed.
shop/bought_coffee_3	You drink it standing up, like everyone else does, and feel almost respectable.
shop/bought_cordial_1	Sweet, thin, and faintly of last summer. It does you more good than it should.
shop/bought_cordial_2	Cordial out of the big jar. Your grandmother made it better, but everyone's did.
shop/bought_cordial_3	You drink it straight down like a child and feel briefly about nine years old.
shop/bought_doughnut_1	Rose jam. Actual rose jam, not the cheap stuff. You take your time over it.
shop/bought_doughnut_2	The sugar goes everywhere. Worth it.
shop/bought_doughnut_3	You eat it in three bites and regret finishing it immediately.
shop/bought_energy_1	An energy drink. Heart does a drum solo, but the tiredness lifts.
shop/bought_energy_2	Energy drink. Wings not included. The jitters are.
shop/bought_energy_3	Cheap energy drink. Taurine, sugar, and pure hope.
shop/bought_fags	A pack of ten. You've got %1 now. Don't smoke them all at once.
shop/bought_fruitspirit_1	Somebody's homemade fruit spirit. Could strip paint. Delicious.
shop/bought_fruitspirit_2	Homemade fruit liqueur. Grandma's recipe, probably illegal.
shop/bought_fruitspirit_3	Fruit spirit. Sweet for a second, then it kicks like a mule.
shop/bought_herring_1	Oily, salty, sharp. Proper food, and it sits in you properly too.
shop/bought_herring_2	Herring straight out of the tub. Your fingers will smell of it until tomorrow.
shop/bought_herring_3	You eat it with a bit of bread and feel, briefly, like a man with a kitchen.
shop/bought_kebab_1	A proper kebab. For a moment, everything is fine.
shop/bought_kebab_2	Kebab, dripping, enormous. This is happiness, briefly.
shop/bought_kebab_3	Late-night kebab energy at any hour of the day. Glorious.
shop/bought_lighter	A shiny plastic lighter. Full of gas and promise.
shop/bought_milk_1	Cold milk. Your stomach, which has been shouting all morning, goes quiet.
shop/bought_milk_2	You drink the milk standing up. Nobody comments, which is a kindness.
shop/bought_milk_3	Plain milk, and after the week you have had it tastes like a good decision.
shop/bought_moonshine_1	Bootleg moonshine of unknown origin. You can see sounds now.
shop/bought_moonshine_2	Moonshine. Smells like a bonfire and hits like one too.
shop/bought_moonshine_3	Home-distilled spirit. Probably safe. Mostly. Cheers.
shop/bought_noodles_1	You get hot water off somebody and eat it out of the pot with the little fork.
shop/bought_noodles_2	It is mostly salt and steam and it is exactly what you wanted.
shop/bought_noodles_3	Noodles out of a pot on a wall. There are worse dinners, and you have had them.
shop/bought_pickle_1	A pickled cucumber and a hunk of bread. Peasant food. Perfect.
shop/bought_pickle_2	Pickle and bread. Sour, salty, weirdly satisfying.
shop/bought_pickle_3	A gherkin the size of your forearm. Breakfast of champions.
shop/bought_pierogi_1	A tray of little stuffed dumplings. Warm, soft, a hug from inside.
shop/bought_pierogi_2	Dumplings, pan-fried and oniony. You could weep.
shop/bought_pierogi_3	Hot dumplings, six of them, gone in a minute flat.
shop/bought_roll_1	A bread roll. Dry, honest, filling. It'll do.
shop/bought_roll_2	Plain bread roll. Not a feast, but it's food.
shop/bought_roll_3	A roll. Chewy, cheap, and exactly enough.
shop/bought_sausage_1	A grilled sausage in a roll, mustard and all. Magnificent.
shop/bought_sausage_2	Hot sausage in a bun, mustard down your wrist. Worth it.
