bld/intro_1	This is the builder. It makes maps, the people you play as, and the numbers behind the game, and it writes all of it into plain text files the game reads. You do not need to know anything about files. Press enter to hear the rest of this.
bld/intro_2	Maps are built by walking. Stand where you want a bench or a bin or a shop, and tell it to put one there. It takes the spot from wherever you happen to be standing, so there are no numbers to work out, though you can type them if you would rather.
bld/intro_3	Everything you make goes into whichever game you have chosen on the main menu. If that is a mod of your own, it all sits in one folder that you can zip up and send to somebody, and they drop it in and have it. If it is the town the game comes with, be aware that an update will put the original back.
bld/intro_4	Shift and B opens this from anywhere in the game, which is how you get back to it. You will not hear this again, but there is an option in the builder to hear it whenever you like. Everything you build is saved as you go.
bld/ours_warning	%1 came with the game. You can change it, and it is your copy, but be warned: when the game updates it will put the original back and your work on it will be gone. An area you made yourself is never touched. Carry on?
