bld/what_they_are_for	What each file is depends on how a map uses it, not on where it sits. A map's music line plays one across the whole area, its bed line loops one underneath, and a sound source puts one at a spot. Name them without the extension.
bld/group_amb	Background sounds that run all the time, %1 of them. These come with the game.
bld/group_emit	Sounds that come from one spot, %1 of them. These come with the game.
bld/where_music_goes	Music is separate and goes in this folder: %1. Music plays across a whole area; a sound comes from one spot.
bld/how_many_tunes	You have %1 tracks there. A map's music line names one without the file extension.
bld/folder_sounds	Sounds that come from one spot, like a dog or a telly. Folder: %1. You have %2 there.
bld/folder_ambience	Background that runs under a whole area. Folder: %1. You have %2 there.
bld/folder_music	Music for an area. Folder: %1. You have %2 there.
bld/folder_footsteps	Ground surfaces. Folder: %1. You have %2 there. One file is enough for a surface; the game will use it for every step.
bld/folder_voices	What a character sounds like when they speak. Folder: %1. You have %2 there.
bld/copy_mod_path	Copy this mod's folder name to the clipboard
save/things_gone	%1 things in your saved game are not part of this game any more and have gone: %2. That usually means a mod has changed since you last played. Everything else is as you left it.
