howto/chars_9	When you make a rule it tells you what it catches today, so you can hear whether you have put the line in the right place before you commit to it.
howto/chars_10	Anybody you make inside a mod belongs to that mod, words and all, so when you send it to somebody they get the whole person rather than a name with nothing to say.
howto/mods_9	All of it is plain text in the mod's folder, so you can open any of it in a notepad if you would rather work that way. The builder is only a friendlier way in.
howto/mods_10	If you edit one of the areas the game came with, the game marks that file as yours and stops treating your work as something that has gone wrong. It will still be replaced when the game updates, though, so anything you want to keep belongs in a mod of your own.
bld/add_person	Put somebody on this map
bld/which_person	Who? Anybody in the game, whether they came with it or you made them.
bld/person_unfinished	%1, %2 lines still to write
bld/nobody_to_place	There is nobody to put anywhere yet.
bld/when_are_they_here	When are they here?
bld/person_all_day	All day and all night
bld/person_some_hours	Only between certain hours
bld/person_from_hour	From which hour? Nought is midnight, nine is nine in the morning.
bld/person_to_hour	Until which hour? Twenty four means through to midnight.
bld/person_placed	%1 is standing at %2.
bld/person_moved	%1 was already on this map, so they have been moved to %2 rather than a second one being put down.
unwritten/person	Somebody nobody has written anything for yet.
howto/build_11	Check map for problems will tell you if something has ended up outside the walls, or if there is no way in or out yet, which is easily done. You can also have it check as you build, which is off to begin with.
howto/mods_11	Your saved game keeps up with the mod as you build it. If you add a drink or a person, everything you were carrying and everyone you knew stays with the right name rather than sliding onto whatever now sits in that place.
venue/shut_because	%1 is shut. %2 is not about at this hour.
bld/who_runs_it	Who is behind the counter? Anybody in the game, or nobody in particular.
bld/nobody_in_particular	Nobody in particular, use the usual one
bld/shut_question	Should it be shut when they are not about?
bld/open_regardless	No, it is open whether they are there or not
bld/shut_when_away_yes	Yes, shut when they are not about
howto/build_12	You can change the areas the game came with, but you will be warned first, and an update will put the original back. An area you made yourself is never touched by an update.
howto/build_13	It also asks whether the place should be shut when they are not about. That gives you something to build a game around: a shop that closes at ten, or a stand that is only there at lunchtime. If you would rather write your own words for when it is shut, name the line after the place, like place slash sklep underscore shut, and the game will use yours instead of its own.
bld/base_warning	This changes the town the game comes with rather than a mod of your own. You can do it, and it is your copy, but when the game updates it will put the original back and your work will be gone. Anything you want to keep belongs in a mod. Carry on?
bld/base_carry_on	Yes, carry on
bld/base_not_now	No, not now
bld/sounds_need_a_mod	Your own sounds live inside a mod, so there is nowhere to put them until you have one. The game's own sounds are still offered whenever you place a sound on a map. Make a mod from the main menu and this will show you where its five sound folders are.
howto/mods_12	And if you take something out that you were carrying, the game tells you what has gone when you next load, rather than leaving you to notice and wonder whether your save is broken.
carry/offer	You have never played %1, and you have a game going elsewhere. Would you like to bring it across? Your other game is kept exactly as it is, so you can go back to it whenever you like.
carry/start_fresh	No, start this one fresh
carry/could_not	That game could not be brought across, so nothing has been changed.
carry/brought_over	Your game from %1 is here. %2
carry/all_survived	Everything came across.
carry/no_such_character	%1 is not in this town, so you are playing as %2 instead.
carry/no_such_place	There is no %1 here, so you have started at home.
carry/moved_to_entrance	The place you were standing in is smaller here, so you have started at its entrance.
carry/things_missing	%1 things you had are not part of this town and have gone.
mod/base_town	The town the game comes with
howto/mods_13	How the game plays also covers what the street throws at you: how long it leaves you alone between things, how likely something is to happen, and how much busier the night and the busy corners are. A mod can take an event out of its town entirely, so somebody can build a place where nobody ever gets mugged, or where the police never turn up.
howto/mods_14	Nearly everything the game counts is in that file now: the jobs the day gives you, what each is worth and how many you need, what the milestones pay, what a trolley carries and costs, and how fast the police forget you. Between them they decide whether a town is a slog or a doddle, so they are worth a look before you change anything else.
howto/mods_15	The jobs each have their own name, so you can take one out with a single line. A town where nobody smokes has no business asking you to smoke six.
pack/offer_after_making	Would you like the sound pack? It is about four hundred and fifty megabytes of ground surfaces, background noise, sounds you can put at a spot, and music, all there for building with. The game only comes with a handful. You can take it later instead, from the builder.
