howto/mods_16	The game comes with a handful of sounds, which is nowhere near enough to build with. There is a sound pack you can fetch from the builder: a hundred and twenty eight kinds of ground, each with five footsteps, plus a few hundred background loops, sounds you can put at a spot, and music. It is about four hundred and fifty megabytes, so it is not in the game itself.
howto/mods_17	It arrives in eight parts and you can stop it at any point with escape. Whatever has arrived stays, so coming back to it carries on rather than starting again. It lives beside your saved games, so updating the game never wipes it, and you can take it off again from the same screen if you decide you are not building anything after all.
howto/mods_18	Sounds from the pack do not travel with a mod, so whoever you send it to needs the pack as well. Sounds you put in the mod's own folders do travel with it.
